    "privacyPolicy": {
      "value": "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title>Privacy Policy</title>\r\n<style>body{color:#6B7280;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;max-width:900px;margin:40px auto;line-height:1.6}p{margin:0 0 12px;white-space:pre-wrap;}strong{color:#000000 !important;font-weight:700}</style>\r\n</head><body>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">1. INTRODUCTION</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">1.1.</strong>  This privacy policy (&quot;Privacy Policy&quot;) applies to all persons, including visitors, registered users, and service recipients, who visit, access, use, or avail any products or services on or through the FinJ Platform (&quot;Platform&quot;), available at https://www.finj.in/ and its related applications or services, (collectively &quot;Service(s)&quot;), owned and operated by Yellowtork Technology Private Limited, a company incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, with its registered office at Plot No-09, N.E.B Subhas Nagar, Alwar, Rajasthan, India, 301001, (hereinafter referred to as &quot;Yellowtork&quot; or &quot;Company&quot; or &quot;We&quot; or &quot;Us&quot; or &quot;Our&quot;),</p>\r\n<p>&quot;You&quot; / &quot;Your&quot; / &quot;Yourself&quot; refers to any individual who visit, access or uses Platform or its Service.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">1.3.</strong> The Company acts solely as a Lending Service Provider (&quot;LSP&quot;) and owns and operates the Digital Lending Application (&quot;DLA&quot;) accessible through the Platform. In this capacity, the Company acts solely as a facilitator and intermediary between You and the banks, non-banking financial companies, and other regulated entities empanelled on the Platform (collectively, &quot;Lenders&quot; or &quot;Regulated Entities&quot;), through which You may seek financial facilitation, loan origination, and other ancillary services. The Company does not itself sanction, disburse, hold, or service any loan, and does not act as a lender in its own capacity.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">1.4.</strong>  The Company is committed to protecting the privacy and security of Your personal information. This Privacy Policy is intended to provide You with information on how We collect, use, and protect Your personal information and sensitive personal data or information (&quot;Information&quot;) in compliance with the Information Technology Act, 2000, the Information Technology (Reasonable security practices and procedures and sensitive personal data or information) Rules, 2011 (&quot;SPDI Rules&quot;), the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (&quot;DPDPA&quot;), IT (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, Reserve Bank of India (Non-Banking Financial Companies - Credit Facilities) Directions, 2025, and the rules as applicable and made therein as notified from time to time. </p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">2. ELECTRONIC RECORD</strong></p>\r\n<p>This Privacy Policy constitutes an electronic record within the meaning of the Information Technology Act, 2000, and the rules made thereunder. It is published in accordance with applicable law and does not require any physical or digital signature to be valid or enforceable. By accessing the Platform or availing any Service, You acknowledge having read and understood this Privacy Policy.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">3. SCOPE OF CONSENT AND ACKNOWLEDGMENT</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">3.1.  Manner of Consent:</strong> We obtain Your consent through a clear, affirmative action on Your part, such as ticking a consent box, clicking &quot;I agree,&quot; or otherwise actively confirming Your acceptance at the relevant point in Your interaction with the Platform where Your Information is sought.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">3.2 Purpose Disclosure.</strong> We disclose the specific purpose for which Your Information is being collected at the time such Information is sought from You, at such stage of such interface.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">3.3. Audit Trail:</strong> Every instance of consent sought and obtained from You under this Policy is logged and maintained in an auditable record, including the date, time, purpose, and scope of consent granted, for verification and regulatory purposes.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">3.4 You have the right to:</strong> (i) provide or decline consent for specific categories of Information, rather than the Service as a whole; (ii) restrict disclosure of Your Information to specific categories of third parties; (iii) set or modify Your preferred data retention period, subject to statutory minimums; and (iv) revoke consent previously granted, in each case by writing to grievance@finj.in or through the settings available on the Platform. Withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness of any processing carried out before such withdrawal. Where withdrawal limits Our ability to provide a Service that depends on the relevant Information, the consequences of such withdrawal (including discontinuation of that Service) shall be borne by You.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">3.5 Accuracy of Information.</strong> You confirm that the Information You provide to Us is accurate and does not violate or infringe any applicable law, and that You have the lawful right and authority to share such Information with Us (including, where applicable, Information relating to family members, nominees, guarantors, or other third parties as referred)</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">4. ELIGIBILITY</strong></p>\r\n<p>The Services are not intended for users under the age of 18, unless permitted under applicable local laws (Permissible Age). We do not knowingly collect any personal information from users or market to or solicit information from anyone under the Permissible Age. If we become aware that a person submitting personal information is under the Permissible Age, we will delete the account and any related information as soon as possible. If you believe we might have any information from or about a user under the Permissible Age, please contact us at grievance@finj.in.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">5. WHAT INFORMATION IS COLLECTED</strong></p>\r\n<p>We collect Your Information on a need-basis only, for the specific purposes disclosed to You, and do not collect Information beyond what is reasonably necessary for that purpose.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">5.1.  Information collected generally</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong>  When You register to use any Service, We may collect Your first name, last name, email address, mobile number, and location. </p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong>  In the event You register using any social media, We may collect the username associated with the social media You choose to register for any Service.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong>  We may collect Your passwords and other identifier we are lawfully required to collect in relation to authentication or verification of Your identity or credentials in connection with Your account.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)</strong>  We may collect details of family members, legal heirs, nominees, guarantors, joint policyholders, beneficiaries, authorized or habitual drivers, emergency contacts, references, or any other person whose Information is reasonably required in connection with Your registration, insurance, or other non-lending Services.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(e)</strong>  We may collect and maintain records of communications with You for inquiry handling, orders, quality assurance, dispute resolution, training, compliance, and administration of Services, subject to notice and consent where mandated by applicable law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">5.2. Information Collected in Connection with Lending or Credit Services</strong></p>\r\n<p>Where We facilitate any lending or credit-related Service on behalf of a regulated lending partner, We act in a limited capacity and store only the minimum Information necessary for that role - namely, Your name, address, and contact details. Any further Information collected in connection with such Service, including the categories below, is processed on behalf of, and remains the responsibility of, the relevant lending partner:</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong> KYC documents (e.g., Aadhaar, PAN, driving licence, GST certificate) and other identifiers required for identity or credential verification;</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong> Bank account details, credit/debit card details, tokenized payment credentials, and transactional data;</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong> Information relating to any security or asset proposed for hypothecation;</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)</strong> Credit reports and credit information obtained from Credit Information Companies on Your behalf, as further described in Clause5.5 below.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>We do not retain the Information described in this Clause 2.2 beyond what is necessary to transmit it to, or facilitate its processing by, the relevant lending partner, except where continued retention is required under applicable law (including KYC record-keeping requirements).</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">5.3. Biometric Information</strong></p>\r\n<p>We do not collect or store any biometric data, including fingerprints, facial recognition data, or iris scans, except where explicitly permitted or mandated under applicable law for identity verification purposes (such as Aadhaar-based authentication conducted through a UIDAI-licensed intermediary), in which case such data is processed strictly in accordance with applicable statutory requirements and is not retained by Us beyond what is legally permitted.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">5.4. Automatically Collected Data</strong></p>\r\n<p>Certain Information is collected automatically as a function of Your use of the Platform, without requiring a separate consent action at the point of collection, where such collection is necessary for the operation, security, or performance of the Service. This Information may not reveal specific identity but may include the Information set out below.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)  Log and Usage Data:</strong> IP address of the device used, time zone, and operating system, login Information (registration date, date of last password change, date of the last successful login) along with the type and version of Your browser on the basis of Our legitimate interest in maintaining platform security, preventing fraud, and ensuring proper functioning of the Service</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)  Device resource access:</strong> We do not access, and the Platform does not request, permissions to Your device&#x27;s file storage, media gallery, contact list, call logs, or telephony functions. Where access to Your camera, microphone, or location is required, such access is sought only on a one-time basis, solely for the purpose of onboarding and KYC verification, and only with Your explicit consent at the time such access is sought. You may decline any such permission, though this may limit Our ability to complete onboarding or KYC.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)  Clickstream Data:</strong> Information about Your activity on Our websites and applications, which includes the websites from which You accessed Our Service, date and time stamp of each visit, searches performed, listings or advertisements You clicked, duration of Your visit and the order in which You visit the content on Our website or application, is collected to operate and improve Our Service.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)  Cookies and Tracking Technologies:</strong> We use cookies, pixel tags, web beacons, mobile device IDs, and similar technologies to collect information regarding Your use of the Platform. These technologies help Us personalise Your experience, analyse usage trends, prevent fraud, and improve Our Services. Where such technologies involve the collection of personal data, We will seek Your explicit consent before collecting such data from You. You may withdraw such consent at any time by writing to Us at grievance@finj.in.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">5.5. Information obtained from Credit Information Companies on your behalf</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong>  We may obtain Your credit reports from credit information companies registered under the Credit Information Companies (Regulation) Act, 2005 (&quot;CICs&quot;) on Your behalf. We may process these credit reports further and then share Credit Information Aggregates with our lending partners. By consenting to use and avail Your credit report through Us, You agree that Company shall be entitled to rely on Your authorisation and consent granted by You to Us, and authorised to share Your Personal Information with CICs and regulated entities.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong>  We shall not transmit, sell or rent credit reports to any other third party and the same cannot be copied or reproduced other than as agreed herein. Credit reports provided to Us are solely the property of the CICs and You.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">6. HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION</strong></p>\r\n<p>As described in Clause3.2, We disclose the specific purpose for which Your Information is sought at the point of collection. We collect and process Your Information to the extent permissible under applicable law. We have set out below a description of the purposes for which We use Your Information and the specific Information for each listed purpose.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">6.1.  To provide access and inform You about various Services offered by Us.</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong>  If You log in using Your mobile number or email id, We use Your first name and last name, mobile number, and/or email address to identify You as a user and provide access to Our websites and applications.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong>  We use clickstream data to offer You tailored content, such as giving You more relevant search results when using Our Services.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong>  We may process Your Information for lawful business purposes including but not limited to compliance checks, insurance, lending (through third parties notified as digital lenders), and mobility solutions resale through Our group companies. For any purpose not described in this Policy, We will notify You and seek fresh consent where required by law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)</strong>  We may process Your Information for providing You with banking or non-banking services from our lending partners, financial reporting through partner regulated entities for audit and record keeping purposes.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">6.2.  To send You survey and marketing communications.</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong>  Subject to Your consent as described in Section 5, We may share Your Information with select partners in the course of Our business, who have agreed to respect and protect Your privacy. These selected partners may use Your Information to deliver Services tailored to Your preferences and interests.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong>  We may contact You through Your registered mobile number or email id to take feedback from You about Our Services.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong>  We may contact You using Your email id or mobile number to share various products and Services that may be of interest to You or to address queries or resolve any concerns You may raise.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)</strong>  You can ask Us to stop sending You such marketing communication at any time by: (i) clicking on the opt-out link in the email sent to You; (ii) changing Your notification settings in Your account; or (iii) by stating to Our calling agent that You do not wish to be contacted.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">6.3.  To review performance of Our websites and undertake measures to prevent fraud and security breaches.</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong>  We use Your mobile number, log data, and unique device identifiers to administer and protect Our websites (including troubleshooting, data analysis, testing, fraud prevention, system maintenance, support, reporting, and hosting of data).</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong>  To prevent and detect fraud on Our Services, We make use of algorithms that recognize suspicious or fraudulent user behaviour based on certain information, such as user activity and posted content, which may lead to Us banning certain user accounts.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong>  We collect certain Information from and in relation to the electronic device from which You are accessing Our Services based on Our legitimate interest in preventing fraud. The Information We collect includes Your user ID, IP address, device language settings, device brand and type, device operating system and version, browser type and version.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">6.4. To provide customer support.</strong></p>\r\n<p>We use Your personal information (including Your mobile number and email address) to respond to Your queries, process Your requests, and resolve concerns relating to Your account or the Services.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">6.5. To comply with legal and regulatory requirements.</strong></p>\r\n<p>We may use Your Information to respond to requests, summons, or orders from courts, regulators, law enforcement agencies, or other government authorities, and to comply with applicable law, including reporting obligations under RBI directions and the Prevention of Money-Laundering Act, 2002.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">7. WHO DO WE SHARE YOUR INFORMATION WITH</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">7.1.</strong> We may transfer or disclose Your Information to the parties set out below on a need-to-know basis for the purposes outlined above.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a) Group Companies:</strong> We may share Your Information with Our group companies, which help Us in providing business operation Services such as product enhancements, customer support, and fraud detection mechanisms.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b) Lending Partners:</strong> We may share Your Information with third parties notified as lenders for the purpose of providing You with lending services. A list of Our current Lending Partners and other third-party service providers, along with the capacity in which each operates, is maintained at [www.finj.in/partners] and updated from time to time. We encourage You to review their privacy policies for details on how they independently process Your Information.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c) Third Party Service Providers:</strong> We use third party service providers to help Us deliver certain aspects of Our Services, such as cloud storage, payment processing, KYC and identity verification, and analytics. We do not allow them to use Your Information for their own purposes.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d) Advertising and Analytics Providers:</strong> To improve Our Services, We may share Your non-identifiable Information with analytics providers that help Us analyse how people are using Our Services.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(e) Governmental Authorities, Statutory Regulators and Investigatory Bodies:</strong> We may disclose Your Information to law enforcement authorities, regulators, governmental or public bodies, and other relevant third parties to comply with any legal or regulatory requirements.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(f) Business Restructuring:</strong> We may choose to sell, transfer, or merge parts of Our business or Our assets. If a change happens to Our business, then the new owners may use Your Information in the same way as set out in this Privacy Policy.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">7.2.</strong> The Company shall not disclose Your Information to any third party without Your prior consent, unless such disclosure is required by applicable law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">7.3.</strong> The Platform may contain links to third-party websites or services not affiliated with Us. We recommend reviewing the privacy policy of any such site before use. Use of any such third-party service is at Your own risk and the Company is not liable for the independent actions of such parties.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">8. DATA SECURITY</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">8.1.</strong>  The Company has implemented and maintains reasonable security practices and procedures, including administrative, physical, and technical safeguards, to protect Your Information from unauthorized access, use, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. These include robust safeguards such as encryption, access control policies, firewalls, and regular security audits. Our security measures are in compliance with the SPDI Rules and the DPDPA (to the extent applicable) and are regularly reviewed and updated.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">8.2.</strong>  Please note, despite the measures We have implemented to protect Your Information, the transfer of Information through the internet or other open networks is never completely secure and there is a risk that Your Information may be accessed by unauthorized third parties.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">8.3.</strong> Our technology systems and those of any party engaged in connection with Our Services comply with applicable cybersecurity and technology standards prescribed by the Reserve Bank of India and other relevant regulatory authorities, as updated from time to time.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">8.4.</strong> In the event of a personal data breach, We will notify the Data Protection Board of India and affected Data Principals as required under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and take prompt remedial measures to contain and investigate the breach.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">9. YOUR RIGHTS</strong></p>\r\n<p>You may exercise the rights set out below in respect of Your Information, subject to applicable law and the terms of this Policy.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)  Right to Not Provide Information:</strong> You have the option to not provide the Information requested by the Company. However, failure to provide essential Information may prevent the Company from offering certain Services to You.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)  Right to Access and Portability:</strong> You have the right to access your Information and request a copy of Your Information from the Company for sharing with third parties.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)  Right to Review and Correct:</strong> You have the right to review the Information You have provided and to request correction or amendment of any inaccurate or deficient Information.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)  Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> You have the right to withdraw Your consent at any time by submitting a written request to the grievance officer. Upon withdrawal, the Company will cease to process unless such processing is required under applicable law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(e)  Right to Request Deletion (&quot;Right to be forgotten&quot;):</strong> You have the right to request the deletion of Your personal data at any time by submitting a written request to the grievance officer.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(f) Right to Nominate:</strong> You have the right to nominate any other individual to exercise Your rights under this Clause9, in the event of Your death or incapacity, by submitting a written request to Our Grievance Officer. Such nomination shall include the nominee&#x27;s name and contact details, and may be modified or revoked by You at any time in the same manner.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(g) Mechanism to Exercise These Rights</strong></p>\r\n<p>You may exercise any of the rights set out in this Section by writing to Our Grievance Officer. Please include Your registered mobile number/email, customer/loan reference number (if any), and the right You wish to exercise, so We can verify and process Your request. Resolution timelines and escalation options are set out in Clause 13.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10. DATA RETENTION</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10.1.</strong>  We retain Your Information for as long as is necessary to fulfil the purpose for which it was collected, to comply with applicable law, or for Our legitimate business and record-keeping purposes, whichever period is longer. We shall not use Your Information for any purpose other than the purpose(s) for which it was collected and disclosed to You, except where You have provided fresh consent for an additional purpose, or where further use is permitted or required under applicable law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10.2.</strong>  Your Information shall be deleted or anonymized in the event the Company ceases to have a legitimate business or legal requirement for processing Your Information.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10.3.</strong>  All Information collected under this Policy is stored on servers located within India. Where any Information is processed outside India in the course of providing the Services, such Information shall be deleted from the servers located outside India and returned to servers within India within twenty-four (24) hours of such processing being completed.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10.4.</strong> In case the Information cannot be deleted (for example, due to storage on backup archives), the Company shall endeavour to securely store the Information and isolate it from further processing until deletion is possible.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10.5.</strong> Subject to applicable law, We retain Your Information for the following periods: </p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong> KYC and identity verification documents - 5 years from the closure of Your last active Service with Us, or as mandated under applicable RBI/KYC regulations, whichever is longer; </p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong> Loan application, sanction, transaction, and repaymentrecords - 8 years from the date of final settlement, in line with statutory record-keeping requirements; </p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong> login, device, and usage data - 12 months from the date of collection; </p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(d)</strong> marketing preference data until You withdraw consent or close Your account. </p>\r\n<p>On expiry of the applicable retention period, Your Information shall be securely deleted or anonymized, except where continued retention is required by law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">10.6. Your Rights.</strong> You may, at any time: (i) request details of the retention period applicable to Your Information; and (ii) request erasure of Your Information, or withdraw consent, subject to Our right to retain it where required by law or to perform a contract with You. Requests under this Section will be handled in accordance with the timelines and escalation process set out in Section 14.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">11. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</strong></p>\r\n<p>You expressly understand and agree that the Company shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary damages, including damages for loss of data or other intangible losses, resulting from: (i) unauthorized access to or alteration of Your Information by third parties despite reasonable security measures being in place; or (ii) any disclosure of Information arising from circumstances beyond the Company&#x27;s reasonable control.</p>\r\n<p>Nothing in this Clause limits any right You may have under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 or any other applicable law.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">12. INDEMNITY</strong></p>\r\n<p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Company, its officers, employees, and affiliates from and against any claims, losses, liabilities, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or in connection with:</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong> any inaccuracy, misrepresentation, or falsity in the Information provided by You to the Company, including Information relating to third parties such as family members, nominees, or guarantors provided by You;</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong> Your unauthorised sharing of another person&#x27;s personal data with the Company without their knowledge or consent; or</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(c)</strong> Your breach of any obligation or representation under this Privacy Policy.</p>\r\n<p>The Company shall not be liable for any consequence, loss, or liability arising from Information provided by You that is inaccurate, incomplete, or unlawfully obtained.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">13. DISCLAIMER</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">13.1.</strong> In case any personal data is shared by You with Us which was not requested by Us during reistration, We will not be liable for any breach or disclosure in relation to such data.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">13.2.</strong> While We take reasonable steps to ensure the accuracy of information on the Platform, We do not warrant that all information is complete, current, or error-free. You are encouraged to verify any information that is material to Your decision to avail any Service.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">13.3.</strong> If You have any questions regarding this Policy or the protection of Your personal data, please contact Us at grievance@finj.in.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">14. GRIEVANCE REDRESSAL</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">14.1.</strong> In case of any grievances relating to the processing of Your Information or this Privacy Policy, You may contact Our designated grievance officer:</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">Email: grievance@finj.in</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">Address: Plot No-09, N.E.B Subhash Nagar, Alwar, Rajasthan, India, 301001</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">14.2.</strong> We will acknowledge Your grievance promptly and endeavour to resolve it within thirty (30) days of receipt. In any event, We shall resolve Your grievance no later than ninety (90) days, as required under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">14.3.</strong> If You are not satisfied with the resolution provided, or do not receive a response within thirty (30) days, You may escalate Your grievance to:</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(a)</strong> the Reserve Bank of India&#x27;s Complaint Management System (https://cms.rbi.org.in), the Sachet Portal, or the Centralised Receipt and Processing Centre, 4th Floor, Reserve Bank of India, Sector 17, Central Vista, Chandigarh - 160017 (for lending-related grievances); or</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">(b)</strong> the Data Protection Board of India (for grievances relating to processing of Your Information).</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">15. GOVERNING LAW</strong></p>\r\n<p>This Privacy Policy is governed by the laws of India. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Policy, which is not resolved through the grievance mechanism in Clause 13, shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the courts at Delhi, India, and where applicable, the dispute resolution mechanism set out in the Terms and Conditions.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">16. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">16.1.</strong> We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Minor changes (such as typographical corrections or contact detail updates) will be reflected by updating the &quot;Last Updated&quot; date on this page without prior notice.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">16.2.</strong> Where a change materially affects how We collect, use, or share Your Information, We will notify You by a prominent notice on the Platform or by email to Your registered email address, at least fifteen (15) days before it takes effect. Where a change requires Your fresh consent, We will seek it separately before the change applies to You.</p>\r\n<p><strong style=\"color:#000000\">16.3.</strong> Your continued use of the Platform after notice of a change constitutes Your acceptance of the updated Policy. </p>\r\n</body></html>\r\n",
      "lastUpdatedAt": "2026-08-11T05:32:50.984Z"
    },
